{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["ASM-1 and ASM-16: the procurement source is a mock adapter containing representative PO and receiving records; no live external connector is required.","ASM-3 and ASM-12: forecasts use dated feeding plans, apply configured wastage to estimated consumption, and mark periods without plans unavailable.","ASM-4 and ASM-13: a movement that would make inventory negative is refused and the resulting shortage is shown by the web app when returned by the service.","ASM-5 and ASM-14: projected ship date uses the current date plus days needed to reach target weight at current ADG, with no date for zero or negative ADG.","ASM-6 and ASM-15: date, breed, sex, and pen filters are on the dedicated Feed-to-Gain report, and export retains the selected scope.","ASM-7: feeding and weight records can be edited or voided, affected balances and metrics are recalculated, and original records remain in history.","ASM-8 and ASM-19: gain assumptions are per lot and one configurable yard-level target weight applies to all lots.","ASM-9 and ASM-18: calculations use pounds and one configured currency, supported ton-based prices convert to per-pound display and calculation values, and ration proportions are as-fed.","ASM-10: receiving head count remains fixed for the requested metrics; later transfers, deaths, or sales are not accounted for.","ASM-17: daily plan quantity is the entered per-animal rate multiplied by pen animal count.","ASM-20: record metadata includes creator and last-changer identifiers and timestamps, without a full audit trail; the app displays those values when returned.","ASM-2 and ASM-11 provide conflicting repeated-import reconciliation policies; this web spec does not choose a backend policy and assumes the UI displays the service's returned result or conflict details.","ASM-21 and ASM-22: supported browsers are the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and the main flows target WCAG 2.1 AA."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"Pass the core operational flows in 8 browser/version combinations (4 browsers × latest 2 versions).","text":"Support the latest two released versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox for the responsive web app."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"100% of applicable WCAG 2.1 AA success criteria for the main flows pass an accessibility audit.","text":"Meet WCAG 2.1 AA for the main operational flows."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"At the 390 CSS-pixel phone viewport, primary touch targets are at least 44 × 44 CSS pixels.","text":"Keep primary interactive controls touch-sized on narrow layouts."}],"outOfScope":["API-SIDE for this web specification: durable persistence, database schema and seeded rows; procurement source retrieval and import reconciliation policy; transactional stock validation and inventory decrement; server-side ration, allocation, cost, weight, forecast, and feed-to-gain calculations; and recalculation after edits or voids. The web app criteria cover requests sent and API-returned values and messages rendered on screens; the separate API run must prove server behavior."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A browser has no authenticated session","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the shared workspace without a sign-in screen","when":"a user opens the app link"},{"given":"Two browser sessions open the shared workspace","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the same operational controls in both sessions","when":"each session views the same operational record"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide access to the shared workspace without a sign-in screen and present the same operational access level to all users without role-specific permission choices.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-3","I-4","I-5","I-6","I-7","Q-1","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The mock source adapter is configured with PO and receiving records","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"the request contains PO line, vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, and source fields","when":"a user starts synchronization"},{"given":"The mock source adapter returns procurement and receiving records","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, and source values","when":"the synchronization result is displayed"}],"ears":"When a user starts a mock procurement synchronization, the Feedlot web app shall send PO and receiving data requests to the mock source adapter and display the returned procurement and receiving fields.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-7","ASM-1","ASM-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A PO line and source pen records are displayed","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows each lot linked to its PO line and each pen with its ID, capacity, and returned current animal count","when":"a user maps the PO line to multiple lots and assigns those lots to pens"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall let users map one PO line to one or multiple lots and map lots to pens while displaying PO-line traceability, pen ID, capacity, and current animal count returned by the source.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot forecast response contains a target weight, a positive ADG, and a projected date","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned target weight and projected date","when":"the lot forecast is opened"},{"given":"A lot forecast response contains a zero or negative ADG and no projected date","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"ui","then":"the projected-date field is empty on the screen","when":"the lot forecast is opened"}],"ears":"When lifecycle forecast data is returned, the Feedlot web app shall display each lot's target weight and projected market or ship date, leaving the date empty when the returned ADG is zero or negative.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-5","ASM-5","ASM-8","ASM-14","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory response contains feed item details and stock movement totals","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned item fields and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values","when":"a user opens the inventory view"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide an inventory view showing each feed item's name, category, available quantity, unit of measure, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, opening stock, stock received, stock consumed, and closing stock.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory service returns a refusal and shortage amount for a movement that would create a negative balance","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned error and shortage value and keeps the movement form displayed","when":"the user submits that movement"}],"ears":"When a stock movement response refuses a movement that would make available inventory negative, the Feedlot web app shall show the returned shortage error and leave the movement form available for correction.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-4","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The forecast response contains balance and shortage estimates for all six horizons","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual values","when":"a user opens inventory forecasts"},{"given":"A forecast response marks a period without a dated feeding plan as unavailable","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows that period as unavailable rather than showing a numeric estimate","when":"the forecast is displayed"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide inventory forecasts for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons using dated feeding-plan demand, configured wastage for estimated consumption, and an unavailable state for periods without a plan.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-3","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user enters a ration and multiple ingredient quantities or proportions","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the ration fields and returned cost per pound","when":"the ration is saved and returned"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall let users create and view rations with a name, type, ingredient quantities or as-fed proportions, dry-matter percentage, energy value, intended animal type or weight range, and calculated cost per pound.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-9","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The comparison response contains ration costs and associated lot performance values","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows each compared ration's cost per pound and its returned performance values","when":"a user opens ration comparison"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide a ration comparison view showing returned cost per pound alongside returned weight-gain or feed-to-gain performance for lots using the compared rations.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-5","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen, ration, per-animal daily rate, and animal count are entered","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the planned quantity equal to the entered rate multiplied by the animal count and displays the returned plan fields","when":"the user generates a feeding plan"},{"given":"A plan response contains a status","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"the status field shows the returned value, including Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped when returned","when":"the plan is displayed"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall let users generate a dated pen feeding plan from a selected ration, per-animal daily bunk rate, and animal count, and display planned quantity, quantity per animal, planned time, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and plan status.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen contains multiple lots","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen provides a planned-quantity field for each lot and shows a reconciliation flag when the allocation total differs from the plan total","when":"a user creates or edits its feeding plan"},{"given":"A pen contains one lot","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the single lot allocation field","when":"a user creates its feeding plan"}],"ears":"When a feeding plan is for a pen containing multiple lots, the Feedlot web app shall require a planned quantity allocation for each lot and flag allocations that do not reconcile with the plan total.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A feeding event response contains planned and actual quantities, variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, and status","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows those returned fields and the inventory decrement equals the actual delivered quantity without adding forecast wastage","when":"the event is saved"}],"ears":"When a user saves an actual feeding event, the Feedlot web app shall display the returned planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, actual-minus-planned variance, feed cost, energy value, inventory consumption, and feeding status, with actual inventory decrement based on delivered quantity rather than wastage-adjusted estimated consumption.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-3","ASM-9","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen plan has multiple lot allocations and the saved event response contains actual lot quantities and event cost","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows each lot's returned actual quantity and the event cost returned for the save","when":"the feeding event details are opened"}],"ears":"When a saved feeding event has multiple planned lot allocations, the Feedlot web app shall display the returned actual-quantity allocation to each lot in proportion to planned quantities and the event cost based on ingredient unit costs recorded at save time.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-7","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user enters an average weight and number weighed","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows total measured weight equal to average weight multiplied by number weighed and shows no independent total-weight input field","when":"the measurement form is displayed and the values are entered"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall let users record a lot weight measurement with measurement date, number of animals weighed, average animal weight, and notes, calculate total measured weight as average weight multiplied by number weighed, and provide no independent total-weight entry field.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The lot response contains multiple dated weight measurements","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a dated list of the returned measurement records and their weight fields","when":"a user opens the lot weight history"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall display each lot's weight measurement history as dated records including average weight, number weighed, and total measured weight.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot metrics response contains the requested feed-to-gain fields","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows each returned metric and the returned feed-cost-per-gain value","when":"a user opens the lot performance view"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall display returned lot feed-to-gain metrics for days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, feed cost per unit of weight gain, and projected ship date using recorded feed costs only for feed cost per unit of gain.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-5","ASM-5","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A saved feeding or weight event is followed by a response containing updated metrics and insights","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the updated metric values and returned next-step suggestions without requiring the user to re-enter the event","when":"the event-save flow completes"}],"ears":"When a feeding or weight event is saved and updated metrics or predictive insights are returned, the Feedlot web app shall refresh the displayed lot metrics and show returned feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestions.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-3","I-4","ASM-7","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The dashboard response contains operational and performance data","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each requested dashboard measure and identifies the returned best and worst performing lots","when":"a user opens the dashboard"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide an operational dashboard showing active lots, active pens, animals per lot and pen, feed inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed, total feed cost, starting and current weight, total weight gain, average daily gain, feed-to-gain ratio, feed cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best and worst performing lots.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The operational report response contains rankings and variance data","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned highest-consuming pen, best feed-to-gain lot, highest-ADG lot, most-used ration, feeding alignment, overfed or underfed pens, remaining inventory, and cost-per-gain values","when":"a user opens operational reports"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide operational report views that identify the highest-feed-consuming pen, best feed-to-gain lot, highest-ADG lot, most-used ration, plan-versus-actual alignment, overfed or underfed pens, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Multiple lot results are returned","id":"AC-REQ-20.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows ADG, FCR, and cost-of-gain fields for the returned lots and date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters","when":"a user opens the Feed-to-Gain report"},{"given":"The Feed-to-Gain report is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-20.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the selected filter values and the results returned for that scope","when":"a user changes a date-range, breed, sex, or pen filter"}],"ears":"Where the dedicated Feed-to-Gain report is open, the Feedlot web app shall compare ADG, FCR, and cost of gain across lots and provide date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-6","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Feed-to-Gain report is filtered to a selected scope","id":"AC-REQ-21.1","level":"ui","then":"the downloaded file is a CSV containing the displayed report results and selected scope","when":"the user exports CSV"},{"given":"A Feed-to-Gain report is filtered to a selected scope","id":"AC-REQ-21.2","level":"ui","then":"the downloaded file is a PDF containing the displayed report results and selected scope","when":"the user exports PDF"}],"ears":"When a user exports the Feed-to-Gain report, the Feedlot web app shall provide CSV and PDF files containing the report results for the selected filter scope.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The yard summary response contains aggregate values for active lots","id":"AC-REQ-22.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost","when":"a user opens the yard-level summary"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide a yard-level summary showing aggregate total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across active lots.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A saved feeding or weight record is available for correction","id":"AC-REQ-23.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the revised balances and metrics and the original record in the record history","when":"the user edits or voids the record and the service returns revised data"}],"ears":"When a user edits or voids a saved feeding or weight record, the Feedlot web app shall display the returned revised balances and metrics while retaining the original record in the record history.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","I-5","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A record response contains creator and last-change identifiers and timestamps","id":"AC-REQ-24.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the returned creator, last-changed identifier, and timestamps without a full audit-log view","when":"the record detail is opened"}],"ears":"Where a record detail is displayed, the Feedlot web app shall show returned created-by and last-changed-by identifiers and timestamps without presenting a full audit log.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-4","I-5","ASM-20"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An inventory item or ration has a ton-denominated price and the configured currency is available","id":"AC-REQ-25.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the equivalent per-pound price in the configured currency and quantities in pounds","when":"the item or ration is displayed"}],"ears":"Where inventory or ration screens display ton-denominated prices, the Feedlot web app shall display the equivalent per-pound price in the configured currency and display calculation quantities in pounds.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-5","I-6","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens the project presentation page","id":"AC-REQ-26.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a section for each requested presentation and delivery topic, including architecture diagrams and demo walkthrough","when":"the page is rendered"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide a project presentation page containing the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo walkthrough, vibe-coding super prompt and other prompts, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market strategy and analysis.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Each app page is rendered at 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900 viewport sizes","id":"AC-REQ-27.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen has no horizontal overflow and controls at the 390x844 viewport measure at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels","when":"the page layout is inspected at each viewport"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall render every page responsively for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths with no horizontal page overflow and touch-sized controls on narrow layouts.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-3","I-4","I-5","I-6","I-7","ASM-21"]}],"suggestions":[]},{"assumptions":["The demo import uses representative PO and receiving records from a mocked source adapter; no live procurement connection is required (ASM-1, ASM-16).","Import conflict behavior is specified only for displaying conflict results. ASM-2 describes updating source-owned fields while preserving mappings, while ASM-11 describes rejecting changed or conflicting imports; these server-side reconciliation assumptions conflict and require resolution outside this web-side spec.","Forecast screens use dated feeding plans, apply configured wastage to estimated demand, and mark periods without plans unavailable (ASM-3, ASM-12).","The UI displays a shortage and an unsaved state when the inventory service refuses a negative-balance movement (ASM-4, ASM-13).","A lot-specific target and gain assumption are used when available; the configured yard target supplies a missing procurement target (ASM-8, ASM-19).","Projected ship dates use the current date and remaining target weight divided by positive ADG; no date is displayed for zero or negative ADG (ASM-5, ASM-14).","Feed cost calculations use pounds and one configured currency, with supported ton-based prices converted to per-pound values (ASM-9).","Receiving head count remains fixed for the requested metrics; later transfers, deaths, and sales are not represented (ASM-10).","Ration ingredient proportions are as-fed, and a pen's plan quantity uses per-animal daily rate multiplied by animal count (ASM-17, ASM-18).","Date, lot, pen, breed, and sex filters are on the dedicated feed-to-gain report, and exports retain that report's selected scope (ASM-6, ASM-15).","Users can access the shared workspace without sign-in and have the same access level (Q-1, Q-6).","Saved feeding-event costs use the ingredient unit costs recorded at event save time (Q-8)."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"Verify layouts at viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1280 CSS pixels; every primary touch target is at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels at 320 pixels wide.","text":"The responsive web app shall render its core pages at phone, tablet, and desktop widths and provide touch-sized controls at the narrow viewport."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"Pass the core import, inventory, plan, feeding, weight, report, and export flows in 8 browser/version combinations (4 browsers × 2 versions).","text":"The responsive web app shall support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 applicable WCAG 2.1 AA violations in automated checks and manual keyboard checks of the import, inventory, plan, feeding, weight, and report flows.","text":"The responsive web app shall meet WCAG 2.1 AA on the main operational flows."}],"outOfScope":["Server-side persistence, transaction atomicity, durable inventory and metric recalculation, and source-record reconciliation outcomes are API-SIDE; this web spec covers the screens' handling and display of returned results.","A live external procurement connector is excluded for the mock-data implementation (ASM-16)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has the shared workspace link and no active session.","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The workspace screen is displayed without a sign-in screen.","when":"The user opens the link in a browser."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall open the shared workspace from its app link without presenting a sign-in gate.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-6"],"stability":0.98},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Two users open the same workspace using separate browser sessions.","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the same available controls for both users.","when":"Both users view the operational and financial screens."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall present the same operational and financial controls to every workspace user without role-specific permissions.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"],"stability":0.98},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The mocked procurement source returns PO and receiving records with representative values.","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned vendor, costs, head count, weights, breed, age, and source fields for the records.","when":"A user starts demo synchronization and opens the imported records list."}],"ears":"When a user starts demo synchronization, the feedlot web app shall display PO and receiving records from the mocked procurement source, including vendor, costs, head count, weights, breed, age, and source.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-7","ASM-1","ASM-16"],"stability":0.91},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An imported PO line and available lots and pens are displayed.","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each PO-line-to-lot-to-pen relationship and the pen ID, capacity, and current animal count.","when":"A user assigns the PO line to multiple lots and assigns those lots to pens."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users map a PO line to one or more lots and map lots to pens while displaying PO-to-lot-to-pen traceability, pen ID, capacity, and current animal count.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The import result contains a duplicate or conflicting-record status and identifies the affected source records.","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each affected record and its conflict status.","when":"The user opens the import results screen."}],"ears":"When the import result identifies duplicate or conflicting source records, the feedlot web app shall display the affected records and a conflict status for operator review.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM--2","ASM-11"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has a receiving date, current weight, gain assumption, and either a procurement target or a configured yard target.","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the selected target weight and projected market date calculated from the current date and days remaining at the gain assumption.","when":"The user opens the lot lifecycle forecast."},{"given":"A lot's gain assumption is zero or negative.","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays no projected market date.","when":"The user opens its lifecycle forecast."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display each lot's target weight and projected market date using its target-weight and gain assumptions, with the configured yard target used when procurement supplies no target.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-5","ASM-5","ASM-8","ASM-14","ASM-19"],"stability":0.82},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Feed inventory records are available, including the listed inventory fields.","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each inventory item with its category, quantity, unit, cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and stock movement values.","when":"A user opens the inventory screen."},{"given":"A user enters values for a new inventory item.","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The inventory screen displays the returned item and its submitted field values.","when":"The user submits the inventory form and the app receives a successful result."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users view and enter feed inventory items and their category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-9"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A stock movement would make available quantity negative and the service returns a refusal with the resulting shortage.","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the shortage and the movement is not shown as saved.","when":"The user submits the movement."}],"ears":"When the inventory service refuses a stock movement because it would make available quantity negative, the feedlot web app shall show the resulting shortage and keep the movement visibly unsaved.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM--4","ASM-13"],"stability":0.88},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Inventory balances, dated feeding plans, and a configured wastage ratio are available.","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays projected ingredient balances and shortages for that horizon using wastage-adjusted estimated consumption.","when":"A user selects each forecast horizon."},{"given":"A forecast period has no feeding plan.","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen marks the period unavailable rather than displaying a projected consumption value.","when":"The user views that period in the forecast."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users configure a wastage ratio and display ingredient balance and shortage forecasts for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons using dated feeding plans and wastage-adjusted estimated consumption.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-3","ASM-12"],"stability":0.88},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user enters a ration with multiple ingredients, as-fed proportions, ingredient costs, and ration attributes.","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each ration's ingredient mix, calculated cost per pound, dry matter percentage, energy value, intended animal type or weight range, and side-by-side cost values.","when":"The user saves and compares the ration with another ration."},{"given":"An ingredient price is supplied per ton and the configured currency and pound conversion are available.","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays its converted per-pound cost and the resulting ration cost per pound.","when":"The user views that ingredient in a ration."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users create and compare rations with as-fed ingredient proportions and display each ration's calculated cost per pound, dry matter percentage, energy value, and intended animal type or weight range.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM--9","ASM-18"],"stability":0.89},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen has an animal count and the user selects a ration, date, feeding time, and per-animal daily rate.","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays planned quantity equal to the per-animal rate multiplied by animal count, along with quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and plan status.","when":"The user generates the feeding plan."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users generate a dated feeding plan for a pen from its selected ration, per-animal daily bunk rate, and animal count, and display planned quantity, quantity per animal, feeding time, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and plan status.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-17"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen contains multiple lots and a feeding plan has a total planned quantity.","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays an allocation reconciliation flag and the difference from the plan total.","when":"The user enters a planned quantity allocation for each lot that does not sum to the plan total."},{"given":"A pen contains multiple lots and an allocation is missing for one lot.","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen identifies the lot without an allocation and does not show the plan as saved.","when":"The user attempts to save the plan."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall require a planned quantity allocation to each lot in a multi-lot pen and flag allocations that do not reconcile with the pen plan total.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-2"],"stability":0.96},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A feeding plan exists for a pen and the user enters an actual delivered quantity and feeding details.","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the submitted activity fields and feed variance equal to actual delivered quantity minus planned quantity.","when":"The user saves the feeding activity and opens its detail screen."}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users log a feeding activity against a pen with feeding date, lot, ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, feed variance, feed cost, energy value, inventory consumed, and feeding status.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A feeding activity delivers 50 pounds, the planned allocation is 60 percent to one lot and 40 percent to another, and the configured wastage ratio is nonzero.","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays an inventory decrement of 50 pounds, wastage-adjusted estimated consumption separately, and lot allocations of 30 and 20 pounds.","when":"The user saves the activity and opens its detail screen."},{"given":"An ingredient unit cost is 0.10 currency units per pound when an earlier event is saved and later changes to 0.12.","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the earlier event cost using 0.10 per pound and the new event 